  "report_sha256": "f55bdcefe556222a5b6043f03591e38f10ad8c76bc3c3c73a8eb45aed73c0ef8",
  "scope": "Two independent identical-policy resumption runs reproduce the same operations, admissions, stored rows, closure and next selections. Both stepwise prefixes compare the complete maintained and rebuilt catalogs, order and activation counts using only then-available rows. Cold replay forbids fresh discovery and reference search, verifies all 3781 reference nodes and reproduces global coverage 66/83. The resumed missing branch reaches a newly acquired Horn and zero-valid terminal through eleven nodes; its sibling reuses three stored nodes but remains open. A new split stores eight nodes on one side and interrupts thirteen entered but unstored states on the other. The union retains nineteen patterns and one split. All 1107 prior manifested artifacts and all 3734 prior reference payloads are unchanged. Preparation, interrupted work, maintenance, export and cold replay costs remain charged. The documented conditional no-progress argument applies to fixed-budget retries on an unchanged deterministic unary dependency chain; it is not a SAT lower bound or a claim that the current chain exceeds a fresh budget of 32. No new Lean theorem, comparative speedup, peak RAM result, holdout estimate or unrestricted-SAT efficiency bound is claimed.",
